on you noted at monarchinitiative.org. Please let me know if any further adjustments are needed.\n\nChanges committed in PR #<NN>.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778616152472,"end":1778616152477}},"id":"prt_e1dc8afa2002iKzrBWR6cH8zms","sessionID":"ses_1e246c2d3ffeM5k7GthnG8NGmd","messageID":"msg_e1dc89280001HE4U7vYHXANkeQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778616154221,"sessionID":"ses_1e246c2d3ffeM5k7GthnG8NGmd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"functions.read:54","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md"},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Summary\n2: \n3: This PR addresses **issue #9933** by completing the missing gene association for **MONDO:0980992 \"Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9\"**. The term already existed with an OMIM cross-reference (OMIM:621512), but the causal gene relationship and corresponding synonyms had not yet been added.\n4: \n5: ## Changes made to MONDO:0980992\n6: \n7: 1. **Added definition** following the `disease_series_by_gene` design pattern:\n8:    > \"Any Meier-Gorlin syndrome in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the GINS3 gene.\"\n9: \n10: 2. **Added exact synonyms**:\n11:    - `GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome` (with `MONDO:design_pattern` and `MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene` sources)\n12:    - `Meier-Gorlin syndrome caused by mutation in GINS3`\n13:    - `Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9` (with DOID and OMIM sources)\n14:    - `Meier-Gorlin syndrome type 9`\n15:    - `MGORS9` (exact abbreviation sourced from OMIM:621512)\n16: \n17: 3. **Added logical definition** (`intersection_of`):\n18:    - `Meier-Gorlin syndrome`\n19:    - `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/25851` (GINS3)\n20: \n21: 4. **Added relationships**:\n22:    - `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/25851 {source=\"OMIM:621512\"}`\n23:    - `has_characteristic HP:0000007 {source=\"MONDO:HPOA\", source=\"OMIM:621512\"}` (Autosomal recessive inheritance)\n24: \n25: 5. **Added term tracker item** linking back to the originating GitHub issue.\n26: \n27: ## Rationale\n28: \n29: The issue reported that while MONDO had a term for Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9 (OMIM:621512), the gene-to-disease association had not yet been included, which is why it was not visible on Monarch Initiative. The curation team confirmed that adding the **GINS3** gene association and the synonym **\"GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome\"** would resolve this. The update follows the same design pattern used by other numbered Meier-Gorlin syndrome terms in MONDO (e.g., MONDO:0009143, MONDO:0013428, MONDO:0014894).\n30: \n31: ## Validation performed\n32: \n33: - [x] Checked out MONDO:0980992 for editing\n34: - [x] Verified **HGNC:25851** is the correct identifier for **GINS3** via HGNC REST API\n35: - [x] Confirmed **OMIM:621512** title includes \"MEIER-GORLIN SYNDROME 9; MGORS9\" via NCBI E-utilities\n36: - [x] Reviewed the `disease_series_by_gene` pattern applied to sibling terms (Meier-Gorlin syndrome 1, 2, 3, 7)\n37: - [x] Edited the term following the established sibling pattern\n38: - [x] Checked the term back into `mondo-edit.obo`\n39: - [x] Ran `make NORM` to normalize serialization\n40: - [x] Ran `robot convert` syntax check — passed with no errors\n41: - [x] Verified the final diff modifies only MONDO:0980992\n42: \n43: ## Background research\n44: \n45: - **PMID:38773883** (cited in the issue) was reviewed via PubMed: *\"Functional studies in yeast confirm the pathogenicity of a new GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome variant.\"* This publication supports the GINS3 gene-disease association.\n46: - The OMIM reference (OMIM:621512) was used as the primary source for the gene relationship, consistent with how other Meier-Gorlin syndrome gene associations are sourced in MONDO.\n\n(End of file - total 46 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nThis PR addresses **issue #9933** by completing the missing gene association for **MONDO:0980992 \"Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9\"**. The term already existed with an OMIM cross-reference (OMIM:621512), but the causal gene relationship and corresponding synonyms had not yet been added.\n\n## Changes made to MONDO:0980992\n\n1. **Added definition** following the `disease_series_by_gene` design pattern:\n   > \"Any Meier-Gorlin syndrome in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the GINS3 gene.\"\n\n2. **Added exact synonyms**:\n   - `GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome` (with `MONDO:design_pattern` and `MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene` sources)\n   - `Meier-Gorlin syndrome caused by mutation in GINS3`\n   - `Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9` (with DOID and OMIM sources)\n   - `Meier-Gorlin syndrome type 9`\n   - `MGORS9` (exact abbreviation sourced from OMIM:621512)\n\n3. **Added logical definition** (`intersection_of`):\n   - `Meier-Gorlin syndrome`\n   - `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/25851` (GINS3)\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"PR_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778616154215,"end":1778616154220}},"id":"prt_e1dc8b2e6001NBe0ThuXF4zUYi","sessionID":"ses_1e246c2d3ffeM5k7GthnG8NGmd","messageID":"msg_e1dc89280001HE4U7vYHXANkeQ"}}
